---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// The club's privacy notice. Every statement here has to be true of the
// system as built: who can read what is set by RLS and column grants (0018),
// and the processors are the services in OPERATIONS.md. Change one, change
// this. The decisions it rests on are listed for the committee in
// roadmap/committee/privacy-and-terms.md.

const contact = 'info@omaghharriers.com';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Notice — Omagh Harriers AC">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-2">Privacy notice</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">Last updated: November 2026</p>

    <div class="prose prose-sm max-w-none text-gray-700 space-y-6">
      <p>
        Omagh Harriers AC (“the club”, “we”) is responsible for the personal information described
        here, as its data controller under UK data protection law. This notice explains what we hold,
        why, who can see it, how long we keep it, and what you can ask us to do with it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Most of our members are children, so this notice is written for <strong>parents and
        guardians</strong> as well as adult members. Where it says “you”, it means the member, or the
        parent or guardian acting for them. It also covers guests who come to a session, and the
        volunteers who run sessions.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">What we hold</h2>
      <p><strong>About each member</strong></p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>Name, date of birth and gender</li>
        <li>Athletics NI registration number, where you have one</li>
        <li>Membership status, and which squads they train with</li>
        <li>Which training sessions they attended, when, and who signed them in</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>About each household</strong></p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>The name and email address of the household's contact</li>
        <li>How the contact signs in to the members' area (an email link, Google or Microsoft)</li>
        <li>
          The household's training credit: money paid in, sessions charged, money handed back,
          corrections and transfers, with the date of each and who recorded it
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>About guests</strong></p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>Name, the sessions they came to, and what they paid on the night</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>About volunteers</strong></p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          The name of the registrar or administrator who recorded each sign-in, payment or correction,
          so that a night's takings can be checked
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We don't hold medical information, bank or card details, or photographs in the members' area.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Where it comes from</h2>
      <p>
        Membership details, including names, dates of birth, gender, Athletics NI numbers and the
        household contact's email, come from <strong>Klubfunder</strong>, the platform you use to join
        the club and Athletics NI. We copy them from Klubfunder and keep them up to date from it.
        Attendance and training credit are recorded by the club's volunteers at training. A guest's
        name is given by the guest at the session.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Why we hold it, and on what basis</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          <strong>Running your membership</strong>, including the members' area and training credit:
          this is necessary for the membership you have with the club.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Recording who was at each session</strong>, members and guests: this is in the
          club's legitimate interests, so that we know who was in our care at a session, can charge
          for it correctly, and can contact the right household if something happens.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Keeping financial records</strong>: the club has to keep accounts, and a household
          needs to be able to check its own statement.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We don't rely on your consent for any of this, and we don't use your information for
        marketing.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Who can see it</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          <strong>Your household's contact</strong> sees your household's members, training credit and
          attendance, and nobody else's.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Registrars</strong>, the volunteers who sign runners in at training, see every
          member's name, which household they belong to, that household's training credit balance,
          and who attended each session. They don't see dates of birth, gender, Athletics NI numbers
          or email addresses. The registrar app keeps a copy of a night's list on the registrar's
          phone, so that it works where there's no signal.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Club administrators</strong>, a small number of committee members, see everything
          described in this notice, so that they can manage membership and accounts. They can download
          attendance and payment reports.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If a phone fails at training, a printed sign-in sheet with members' names and credit balances
        may be used for the night. Volunteers are asked to keep printed sheets and downloaded reports
        secure and to destroy them once they're no longer needed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Who else handles it</h2>
      <p>
        We don't sell or share your information. We share it with Athletics NI only where it's needed
        to register you for competition. These services handle it on our behalf, under contract, and
        only to provide their service:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li><strong>Supabase</strong>, which stores the members' area database, in Ireland</li>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts this website and runs the security check on the sign-in page</li>
        <li><strong>Resend</strong>, which sends sign-in emails</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong> and <strong>Microsoft</strong>, only if you choose to sign in with
          them
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Klubfunder holds your membership record under its own privacy notice, as the platform you
        joined through.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>
          <strong>Members and households</strong>: for as long as you're a member, and for two years
          after your membership lapses, in case you rejoin. After that we remove your name, date of
          birth, gender, Athletics NI number and email address.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Training credit records</strong>: for six years, as the club's financial records.
          Once your details have been removed, these records no longer identify you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Attendance</strong>: kept with your membership record, and stops identifying you when
          your details are removed.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Guests</strong>: removed, with their attendance, a year after the last session they
          came to.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask us to:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
        <li>give you a copy of the information we hold about you or your child</li>
        <li>correct anything that's wrong</li>
        <li>
          delete your information. We'll remove your personal details. Financial records we must keep
          are kept without them, so they no longer identify you
        </li>
        <li>restrict how we use your information, or object to how we use it</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Most details come from Klubfunder, so the quickest way to correct a name, date of birth or
        email is usually to update it there. For anything else, email
        <a href={`mailto:${contact}`} class="underline hover:text-gray-900">{contact}</a>. We'll
        reply within one month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're unhappy with how we've handled your information, you can complain to the
        Information Commissioner's Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" class="underline hover:text-gray-900">ico.org.uk</a>
        or on 0303 123 1113. We'd appreciate the chance to put it right first.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        The members' area uses only the cookies it needs to work: one that keeps you signed in, one
        that remembers your email address for a few minutes while you sign in, and, for
        administrators, one that shows a confirmation after saving a form. The security check on the
        sign-in page is provided by Cloudflare. We don't use advertising or analytics cookies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900">Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        When we change this notice we'll update the date at the top. If a change affects what we hold
        or who can see it, we'll tell household contacts by email or in the members' area.
      </p>

      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 italic">
        Draft for the club committee's approval.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
